 the diversity this season  um  with you know 50 of our cast being  people of color but also the diversity  within the cookout was refreshing for  america to see  do you think aza made the biggest  mistake ever do you think who do you  think is the next house guest to be  evicted if not aza  okay um  maybe azam made the biggest mistake ever  or maybe  she didn't i don't know um what she sees  for herself in this game  i personally think that  oz's hoh was a waste on me because i i  mean  as soon as tiffany left i was like  oz is probably my best bet of winning  this game if i were to sit next to her  in final two so i was not gonna put her  on the block i wasn't gonna touch her if  i had won hoh i was really planning on  taking her fart in this game i wanted to  split up the guys  i'm not sure if the guys can say the  same  um  so i do believe that it was a wasted hoh  and  i think that she will be following me um  but if not her if she is able to win  that veto and she's the sole vote to  evict  i think i will probably see kyland next  what was the hardest moment for you of  the season being in the big brother  house isn't easy we're always warned to  expect the unexpected was it harder than  you thought  um  big bro okay so the game that i intended  to play was different than the game that  i actually played once i saw that there  were five others of me i kind of had to  recalibrate and reconfigure my strategy  in this game  i did want to come in hot i wanted to  come in  and be messy and chaotic but because of  the cookout  i felt like i couldn't um because the  stakes were so much higher at that point  um  what was i gonna say oh yes um  the hardest part of the game for me was  having to balance  what would have benefited my personal  interests in the game and what benefited  the cookout  for example having to send  derek x holm convincing him that he  shouldn't play in chopping block  roulette because i was more in danger of  going home that week than him i didn't  want him to win i didn't want him to  take claire down at that point alyssa  would have been our only option and we  didn't know how likely sb was to put up  one of her closest allies at that time  um  so i i do  i mean keeping dx would have  been excellent for my personal game he  would have never targeted me he would  have never put me on the block but he  had to go home  because  the cookout  who knows if the cookout could have  taken him out  um and here he was being handed to us on  a silver platter and for selfish reasons  i didn't want to give anyone else in the  cookout the benefit of being able to say  that they sent home dx  who is arguably  the strongest competitive threat of this  season  um so i just didn't want to give any  other member the opportunity to add that  to their resume and that is yet another  reason why dx had to go home but because  he was one of the closest people in the  house to me i did feel very conflicted  guilty and emotional that week and that  was probably the hardest moment of the  game for me  who do you want to stay in the house and  who do you want to join you next in jury  um  i  okay  if big d or kailand were to join me in  jury i would not be mad um i feel like  there were numerous instances  when highland  acted more selfishly than the other  members of the cookout for example sarah  beth was supposed to go home that very  first week of jury and what does kailan  do  he wins the hoh even though he was  supposed to throw it to either aza or  tiff so they could have taken that shot  against sb  um and that's just one example of kailan  kind of  doing his own thing and going rogue and  us having to  overcompensate for that so that he  wouldn't be the biggest target in the  house and people would not be gunning  for him  um so because of that and  another thing is i didn't question  kyle's loyalty to the cookout but i  always kind of wondered is kailyn  setting himself up just in case the  cookout fails and i think he was um i  think he was being i think he was being  very diligent about that um so for that  reason i would not mind if thailand you  know  follows me um and then with big d big d  made it very clear that he wanted to be  sent home at final five he was  just there for fame he was just there  for the money and that's kind of a slap  in the face to the game  um which is a game that i love and  respect so much  so  for those reasons yeah i'd like to see  either kailan or big d follow me  you
 

